        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the port and head out onto Lake Titicaca. Many people in the region consider the lake sacred and associate it with the legend of Manco Cápac, the first Inca ruler.\n\nThe first part of the tour takes you to the floating reed islands of the Uros. There are more than 40 islands, all built by local residents. You'll learn how the islands are made and how the community lives. You can also buy souvenirs and take a ride in a traditional reed boat.\n\nThe journey continues to Taquile Island. Its main settlement sits at an elevation of around 3,950 metres. The island is known for its traditional way of life and its weaving. In 2005, UNESCO recognised Taquile's textile art as a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity.\n\nHave lunch on the island. After returning to Puno, transfer to the airport for your flight to Lima. On arrival, you'll be met and taken to your hotel."
    },
